    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 80.88. His matchup against Roki Sasaki is neutralized by the combination of a favorable park factor and, crucially, Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery, which provides **Corbin Carroll** a prime opportunity to hunt for stolen bases\u2014our most critical scarcity category. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (68.84) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.23) are primary starts. **Brice Turang** benefits from a leading-off spot and a favorable stolen base environment against Matthews, while **Mickey Moniak** enjoys a massive 14% boost from a platoon advantage against Leahy, keeping him in the green despite a subpar park factor.\n\nThe benching of **Cole Young** (37.27) remains the most difficult personnel decision of the day. While **Cole Young** benefits from a strong lineup slot (#2), his projection was cratered by the opposing pitcher's high-efficiency metrics (Drew Rasmussen\u2019s 3.19 xERA), pushing him below our mandatory 40-point \"Zebras\" floor for starting consideration. Elsewhere, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** are steady plays, though both bear a \"Lineup Pending\" warning; should their final batting positions drop significantly, their scores will regress, making them monitor-list candidates. We continue to navigate a depleted depth chart with **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all currently sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on our active rotation to perform at their projected levels.",
